00 per year, executives said Thursday. That does not include discounts from Medicaid or other discount programs.\nThat's a huge price tag, but that's not all: BioMarin secured another priority review voucher, which allows a company to get a speedier drug review from the FDA. BioMarin sold its first voucher in 2014 for $67.5 million.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFDA Approves the First Orally Administered Medicine, Genentech’s Evrysdi (risdiplam), for Treatment of SMA in Adults and Children 2 Months and Older (https://www.reddit.com/r/spinalmuscularatrophy/comments/i5lslb)\nciteturn127reddit24 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.3 years ago; Crawled: 6.0 years ago; [Friday August 07 2020] [+13 votes] ... --Evrysdi improved motor function in people living with SMA over a broad spectrum of ages and levels of disease severity, including Types 1, 2, and 3 SMA ... Perfect opportunity to ask if I can replace Spinraza with Risdiplam.\n"
